{"title":"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f33c5e307573deb29ffcae05d5dbae08ab8653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x-3y-z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065dd05cfbeb30346c273949f950938922b4984d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+3y-14z=0, z \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" />, the numerical value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05ddad18af77b397690ba61a2779e6c89854cd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/27435422cc2cfd06990f2ddb02aafb99c978d3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ -20/17\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"429\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05ddad18af77b397690ba61a2779e6c89854cd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> is constant, as the answers imply, we can pick a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and then solve the two linear equations for the corresponding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />.  We can then plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f900f39c366f610e272b389caaa17f9a34c637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> into the expression to get the answer.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127baed0622ba365dca153b0321e5c4758e3b78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - 3y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ef689b95b6ca0c1016970d0b04045873cafa7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3y = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />.  We can solve each equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89385605cebfe24cd5d7a9402a2908b64a012fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> and set them equal, which leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff8108fa92794f88de49de0ea000d0bd7e6408b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - 1 = 14 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"12\" />.  This leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ef689b95b6ca0c1016970d0b04045873cafa7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3y = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6389a3877e2c9d09826aa0c5e5aa564d8c355afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032f27cccecdf4a910a828f10947ec1c01ab61d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is one solution to the intersection of the two planes given.\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0cb28f2dacf9f800dcb37f4a7922f99c7fe840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3, -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> into the expression gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05ddad18af77b397690ba61a2779e6c89854cd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1c21201a5ac586d45c96e7a7fd88e581a956dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25 + 45}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as a parameter, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8fa7f9588e14bbcf0741d32a50312e5b9fdcab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - 3y = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eefc3153e762989c8193f13b5c1c051268cf875f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3y = 14z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />.  Adding the equations leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14bcaf59ba7deee66ffd8804605dca627ccca61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x = 15z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4eef1fedd35cad4fddfdf0573f38050f41ebbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5z$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.  Plugging that into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eefc3153e762989c8193f13b5c1c051268cf875f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3y = 14z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d521427e6d75afbf314724fa5c924ff6b22aef0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5z + 3y = 14z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc135d328ed878a57c14d02b40ef1174fdd59039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />.  Thus, the intersection of the two planes is given by the parametric line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1032bbe58d8e7293fc43c000a1ae477405d8e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5z, 3z, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> varies along all real numbers.\n</p><p>We plug this in to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05ddad18af77b397690ba61a2779e6c89854cd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21fbc8640faeba580906792f726a8f8ef96d9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25z^2 + 45z^2}{10z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME\" title=\"1964 AHSME\">1964 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1964 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1964\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2<